{"type":"message","id":"f0c9d89f","parentId":"962b3fe9","timestamp":"2026-04-18T03:12:11.783Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The main task kanban table (tblP0dMcFARO3jxF) has records with empty fields. Let me check the AI协作看板 which we know from earlier has useful data.\n\nNow let me understand the current state:\n- Current time: 2026-04-18T03:11 UTC (11:11 AM Beijing)\n- Last heartbeat: 2026-04-18T02:11:00Z (about 1 hour ago)\n- Tasks in main task system: Multiple historical tasks, most done\n- AI协作看板 (JkJCboZR5auRW5sGmpFcPXC8nuc) -分工进度跟踪 table has 4 AI agents tracked\n\n\n- 飞书任务 shows various tasks with some still pending\n\nThe main issues I'm seeing are that the shared pool progress library is inaccessible due to a missing table, several historical tasks appear to be in a Dead state based on their timestamps, and the AI协作 kanban has 4 agents with no new Dead tasks. I need to check the 分工进度跟踪 table since it contains the most recent AI status information, and also examine the 天津瑞湾每周核心事项提醒 checklist which currently has one pending item.\n\nThe checklist item about filling out the weekly core attention matters form is due Sunday, and I notice some older tasks from late January still show as pending—those are likely already dead and need to be marked accordingly.\n\nNow I'm calculating the timeout threshold. The last heartbeat was at 02:11 UTC, and the current time is 03:11 UTC, so anything older than 60 minutes from the task list would be tasks that haven't been updated since before 02:11.\n\nLooking at the task timestamps, I can see two tasks stuck in pending states from January that are clearly dead. Beyond those, the rest of the visible tasks from the Aily bot are also lingering without updates. I should update the heartbeat timestamp and document these findings, but first I need to identify the correct progress reporting table since the shared pool task kanban table reference seems incorrect."},{"type":"text","text":"Now 